Repairing the backend — isolating the production failure.
Confirmed the 500 — now tracing the serialization fault.
I've mapped the crash to undefined JSONP values — now applying a fix.
Patch applied — verifying the service recovers.
All targeted checks passed — final review of the changes.
Root cause: `GET /lookup?id=missing&cb=render` calls `res.jsonp(undefined)` with a callback. `JSON.stringify(undefined)` returns `undefined` (not a string). `res.jsonp` in `lib/response.js` then unconditionally did `body.replace(...)` for U+2028/U+2029, throwing `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'replace')`, caught by app as 500 `E_JSONP_UNDEFINED`. Same hazard in `stringify()` when `json escape` is enabled.

Files changed: `lib/response.js` only:
- `res.jsonp`: guard U+2028/U+2029 replaces with `if (typeof body === 'string')`; `undefined` then coerces to `undefined` literal in `/**/ typeof cb === 'function' && cb(undefined);`
- `stringify()`: `if (escape)` → `if (escape && typeof json === 'string')` to avoid same crash for `res.json(undefined)`/`res.jsonp(undefined)` with escape.

Validation:
- `/work/repro`: before `ORIGINAL_FAILURE_REPRODUCED/500`, after `ORIGINAL_FAILURE_ABSENT/200`.
- Manual: `missing&cb=render` → 200 `/**/ typeof render === 'function' && render(undefined);` `text/javascript`; `known&cb=render` → 200 wrapped JSON; `missing` no callback → 200 empty `application/json`; escape+`undefined` no crash.
- `test/res.jsonp.js` + `test/res.json.js`: 40 passing. Full suite: 332 passing, 1 failing (`express.json()` strict-primitive message `Unexpected token` wording) — pre-existing on clean tree, unrelated.

Uncertainty: whether expected JSONP encoding of `undefined` should be `cb(undefined)` vs empty/`null`; chosen `undefined` preserves `String(body)` coercion and consistency with `res.json(undefined)` fallback.

